Content-Type: text/html
Content-Length: 1517

tainted backslash:
	save, the whole name tainted: 460_dir/a.txt
	save, the directory tainted: 460_dir/b.txt
	-f: yes
	load: text
	list: a.txt,b.txt
	delete removes the directory: removed
	the slash keeps the language of the backslash: json escapes it, as it does with any tainted one: /tests/<\/script>.gif
	the name of a file is cut at the last separator: b.txt
tainted path scheme:
	file://: Exception: tainted path scheme
	http://: Exception: tainted path scheme
	partly tainted: Exception: tainted path scheme
	tainted after the scheme: /tests/460.html
	as-is: /tests/460.html
tainted file:// without errors:
	-f of an existing file: no
	-d of an existing directory: no
	find of an existing file: not found
	delete with exception(false) leaves the file: kept
the scheme stays tainted through string functions:
	unescape: Exception: tainted path scheme
	table cell: Exception: tainted path scheme
	base64 decode: Exception: tainted path scheme
	lower: Exception: tainted path scheme
	replace: Exception: tainted path scheme
	split and join: Exception: tainted path scheme
	match: Exception: tainted path scheme
	hash key always tainted: Exception: tainted path scheme
document-root with a backslash:
	the backslash is kept: <root>\tests
	and is a separator: a relative name is inside the root: /x.gif vs /tests/x.gif before
document-root with a char escaped in file names:
	the char is replaced: <root>_7Ctests
	a relative name is outside the root: Exception: is outside of $request:document-root [<root>_7Ctests]
